      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:3:5:6:5",
      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُ أَبَا الْحَسَنِ ( عليه السلام ) عَنِ الْقُطْنِ وَ الزَّعْفَرَانِ عَلَيْهِمَا زَكَاةٌ قَالَ لَا ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Ali Bin Mahziyar, from Abdul Aziz Bin Al Muhtady who said,",
          "‘I asked Abu Al-Hassan<sup>asws</sup> about the cotton and the saffron, ‘Is there <span class=\"iTxt\">Zakāt</span> upon these two?’ He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘No’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "5. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from Ali ibn Mahziyar from ‘Abd ‘Aziz ibn al-Muhtadiy who has said the following: “I once asked abu al-Hassan, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about cotton and saffron if there is Zakat on it. He (the Imam) said, ‘No, Zakat is not due on it.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
